From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ad5xrecon <ad5xrecon@localhost>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] kiln: read Kiln OS API replies and errors of v0.1.0-rc1

Kiln OS v0.1.0-rc1 cleans up its Moonraker endpoints: kernel_retry and
boot_recovery answer the object {"state": "rebooting"} (the JSON-RPC
result itself, no inner "result"), and every Kiln error has an HTTP
status by kind (409 refused because of the printer's state, 503 the root
agent not answering, 400 a bad parameter, 500 a failure) and a reason
for programs at the start of the message, "[printing] A print is
running"; over JSON-RPC Moonraker also sends the reason as the error's
data {"reason": "printing"}. Kiln's Klipper endpoint
printer.ad5x_setup.control puts the reason in front too (always 400,
no data: Moonraker passes Klipper errors on that way).

- MoonrakerError::from_json_rpc takes "[reason] " off the message when
  the data carries the same reason, so every screen that shows a Kiln
  error (Boot into recovery, service restarts) shows the text only;
  kiln_reason() gives the reason. strip_kiln_reason() takes it off a
  message without data.
- Settings > System > Boot into recovery reads result.state.
- The AD5X setup wizard shows printer.ad5x_setup.control refusals
  without the reason.

Tests: the new reply (and the old double result not taken for a
reboot), refusals and the agent timeout as Moonraker now sends them, the
reason taken off only when the data matches, and strip_kiln_reason on
reasons and look-alikes.
